{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1470925577,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDc1MjczNDk5Mw=="},"added":["enhancement"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1471268937,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIzOTgwNjA5MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/701#issuecomment-239806090"},"message":"Few questions and pointers:\n\nYou write \"should not change (other than from None) in its lifespan\": \"lifespan\" of a Dataset object, the dataset on disk?\n\nPlease check out this implementation: https://github.com/hanke/datalad/blob/nf-metaparser/datalad/metadata/__init__.py#L60\n\nIt uses a UUID (if it finds any), the hexsha of the current branch HEAD (if any), or the local path as the last resort. This is done, because for meta data we need identifiers regardless of whether a UUID is available now, or will be in the future.\n\nThese two concepts could be merged to some degree. But it depends on what we want. If we want any ID, we should not call this method/property `UUID`, if we really want a UUID only, we still need a separate ID mechanism for all non-annex things.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1471270787,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIzOTgxMzgyMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/701#issuecomment-239813822"},"message":"I meant in the life time of that python object, that is why lazy loading once should work fine... But if we allow checksum/path, and then it gets uuid (after annex command runs and inits it), it might change that way i guess","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1472115148,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI0MjMyMDk5Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/701#issuecomment-242320996"},"message":"I think, we can (and may be should) have both. The ID, @hanke is talking about, is mainly for identifying a dataset in a way, that is satisfying regarding metadata. Whereas UUID is a property of an annex repository. So, `AnnexRepo` could still have the lazy `uuid` property as proposed by @yarikoptic , while `Dataset` provides a more general ID mechanism, which uses the `uuid` of its underlying `AnnexRepo` instance, if there is any. These are two different things and while we need these dataset identifiers, the uuid is an independently essential property of an annex, represented by an `AnnexRepo` instance.\n\nThis also means, I agree to @hanke 's implementation in #720, with the exception, that it should be enhanced to use `AnnexRepo.uuid` and let this be the one, that lazily loads it from config.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1472115236,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDc2NzEyMTE5NQ=="},"added":["conference agenda item"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1472123877,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI0MjM1MzAxMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/701#issuecomment-242353011"},"message":"@bpoldrack #720 now implements that.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1472138899,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50NzY3NjE2Njg3"},"status":2}]}